**Corollary 55.3 (deterministic and stochastic boundaries).** A deterministic
finite controller is the degenerate case in which $U$ is a singleton and every
$K_s$ is a point mass. The Kbonacci acquisition theorems in the current `dev`
operate at the measurable common-seed layer; the ExactChart frontier operates
at the finite deterministic layer. Their common invariant is source-uniform
execution, while their resource objectives and termination assumptions remain
separate contracts.

